+  "snippet": "  use: [agents({ agents: ['orderAgent', 'refundAgent'], maxDelegations: 3, historyLength: 4 })],\n});",
+  "cause": "The triage agent, which is the one the support chat actually talks to and which delegates order questions to orderAgent, was defined without a `store`, so its session state is only kept in memory and is lost between requests and can never be found again by sessionId.",
+  "evidence": "refundAgent is defined with `store` and its sessions survive being resumed by id, while triage (and orderAgent) had no `store` configured; FileSessionStore/getSnapshot in @genkit-ai/ai requires a configured server store to persist or look up a session by sessionId, so asking a second question in the same conversation after 'My order is A-1001.' cannot find the prior turn's history and the customer has to repeat the order number, even though a single question still works since it needs no prior turn."
